div.p:
Here geō-meowle  = old woman  or widow;
                  bunden-heorde  = with bound locks;
                  hēof  = lamentation;  cf. l. 3143. on rīce wealg  is less preferable than the MS. reading, heofon rēce swealg  = heaven swallowed the smoke.—H.-So. B. thinks Beowulf's widow (geōmeowle) was probably Hygd; cf. ll. 2370, 3017-3021.
